{%- comment -%}
  Email signup — the newsletter and every "Notify me". All of them are
  Shopify customer forms; the tags are what tell them apart in Admin →
  Customers (newsletter vs next-drop, t-shirts…), so no app is needed to
  segment who asked for what.

  id       – unique form id (required)
  tags     – customer tags
  label    – button text (Subscribe)
  tone     – 'olive' for the bone-on-olive tile
  thanks   – success line
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign classes = 'alp-signup'
  if tone == 'olive'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' alp-signup--olive'
  endif
  if size == 'sm'
    assign classes = classes | append: ' alp-signup--sm'
  endif
-%}
{%- form 'customer', id: id, class: classes, data-alp-signup: '' -%}
  <input type="hidden" name="contact[tags]" value="{{ tags | default: 'newsletter' }}">
  {%- if form.posted_successfully? -%}
    <p class="alp-signup__ok" role="status" data-alp-ok>{{ thanks | default: "You're on the list. We'll be in touch." }}</p>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      With script the form posts in the background and this line replaces the
      field in place — the page doesn't reload, so nobody is thrown to another
      form's "thanks" further down the page.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <p class="alp-signup__ok" role="status" data-alp-ok hidden>{{ thanks | default: "You're on the list. We'll be in touch." }}</p>
    <label class="alp-vh" for="{{ id }}-email">Email address</label>
    <input
      class="alp-signup__input"
      id="{{ id }}-email"
      type="email"
      name="contact[email]"
      placeholder="Email address"
      autocomplete="email"
      autocapitalize="off"
      spellcheck="false"
      required
    >
    <button class="alp-signup__btn" type="submit">{{ label | default: 'Subscribe' }}</button>
    <p class="alp-signup__err" role="alert" data-alp-err{% unless form.errors %} hidden{% endunless %}>That email didn't go through. Mind checking it?</p>
  {%- endif -%}
{%- endform -%}
